# Git commits

When creating git commits in this project:

- **Never** add `Co-authored-by:` trailers (Cursor, Copilot, or any AI/tool).
- **Never** add similar attribution lines such as `Signed-off-by: Cursor` or `Assisted-by: ...`.
- Commit messages contain only the human-readable summary and body – nothing that credits AI as co-author.

```text
# ❌ BAD
feat: add wizard

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

# ✅ GOOD
feat: add wizard
```

If a hook or tool tries to append co-author lines automatically, remove them before committing.
